  "description": "A spatial composition of the components — Party A, the third issue card (as supplied) standing in her tray, the case file that serves as the sorting board, Party B and the calendar. The card comes in from Party A’s side and never fades. Only the supplied relationships are drawn, without arrowheads (a causal link only when supplied) and labelled on their connectors; a tracer follows the supplied order, captioned “Sequence as configured (illustrative)”, while the case file enlarges. At the gather the case file shows the grouping: two subject rows, each in its own frame, under the ● agreed and ◆ open column glyphs (equal weight), the third card in the column of its supplied state, with the state’s caption. “Agreed” only means the supplied list marks the issue as agreed between the parties; nothing is decided or proven; no procedure, effect or outcome is shown.",
